      "accessories_to_confirm": ["Appropriate sample stubs and mounting adhesives"]
    }
  ],
  "not_available": [
    {
      "technique": "Micro-computed tomography (Micro-CT)",
      "why_useful": "Micro-CT is the standard non-destructive technique for visualizing and quantifying the internal 3D architecture of porous materials without requiring physical sectioning."
    }
  ],
  "clarifying_question": null,
  "summary": "No listed instrument can perform non-destructive 3D internal imaging of a porous specimen. The ideal technique for this is micro-computed tomography (micro-CT), which is not currently available in the provided list. The ESEM (EQ10) is available for high-resolution surface imaging, but it is not suitable for visualizing internal structures."
}

{
  "measurement_needs": [
    "internal 3D structure of a porous specimen",
    "non-destructive characterization"
  ],
  "objective_met": false,
  "recommendations": [
    {
      "instrument_id": "EQ07",
